The following skills are forks of Superpowers skills, rewritten so their
artifacts land on a tuckit board instead of in markdown files:

  shared/skills/designing-a-slice/      <- skills/brainstorming
  shared/skills/breaking-down-a-slice/  <- skills/writing-plans
  shared/skills/executing-a-slice/      <- skills/executing-plans
  shared/skills/delegating-a-slice/     <- skills/subagent-driven-development
  shared/skills/shipping-a-slice/       <- skills/finishing-a-development-branch
  shared/skills/requesting-a-review/    <- skills/requesting-code-review
  shared/skills/receiving-a-review/     <- skills/receiving-code-review

The prompt templates forked from subagent-driven-development are split across
two of those directories: delegating-a-slice carries implementer-prompt.md,
and requesting-a-review carries the two review prompts
(task-reviewer-prompt.md -> reviewer-prompt.md, and re-review-prompt.md).

Superpowers' remaining skills (test-driven-development, systematic-debugging,
verification-before-completion, using-git-worktrees and
dispatching-parallel-agents) are not forked here. This plugin is meant to replace
Superpowers rather than run alongside it, so it does not defer to them by name;
until they are forked too, the layers they cover are simply absent.
